#glossary-term("Apple Desktop Bus (ADB)")
#para("The connection system used by the original vintage keyboard before its Bluetooth conversion.")
#glossary-term("AtEase")
#para("The PiForma’s folder-like launcher for opening configured programs.")
#glossary-term("Bluetooth LE")
#para("Bluetooth Low Energy, the wireless connection used by the converted keyboard.")
#glossary-term("Chime selector")
#para("The rear dial that chooses a startup sound; some settings are silent.")
#glossary-term("Clippy")
#para("The assistant at the lower-right corner of the desktop. Type a question in its Chat with Clippy window; check its suggestions against the actual setup.")
#glossary-term("Composite video")
#para("The video signal accepted by the rear RCA input, used to show an external source on the PiForma screen. The jack carries video only, not audio.")
#glossary-term("Control Strip")
#para("The small program-launching and window-focus strip supplied by ControlStrip Simulator.")
#glossary-term("Desktop")
#para("The working screen with its background, launchers, menu bar, and application windows.")
#glossary-term("Docs Viewer")
#para("Macintosh PiForma Docs Viewer, the program for reading the project’s hardware, software and maintenance documents, with an offline snapshot. It is separate from About This PiForma.")
#glossary-term("EmulationStation")
#para("The game-list menu of RetroPie, opened from AtEase. It is a separate application from the games it starts.")
#glossary-term("Emulator")
#para("A program that imitates another computer or games system so compatible software can run.")
#glossary-term("Full-screen application")
#para("A program occupying the display, often covering the normal desktop menus.")
#glossary-term("GPIO")
#para("General-purpose input/output pins on the Raspberry Pi, used for controls in this build. Appendix A uses BCM pin numbering.")
#glossary-term("HDMI")
#para("The digital video connection that carries the Raspberry Pi’s picture to the PiForma screen. Select HDMI on the rear source selector to see the Pi.")
#glossary-term("microSD")
#para("The small storage card containing the PiForma’s operating system and saved files.")
#glossary-term("PiForma Panel")
#para("The program that supplies the menu bar across the top of the screen, including the Special menu with Shut Down and Sleep Display.")
#glossary-term("Qi charging")
#para("Wireless charging using an aligned transmitter and receiver.")
#glossary-term("Raspberry Pi")
#para("The small computer board inside the PiForma case.")
#glossary-term("Raspberry Pi OS")
#para("The operating system documented beneath the PiForma’s Macintosh-inspired desktop.")
#glossary-term("RetroPie")
#para("The games/emulation environment, opened through EmulationStation in this setup.")
#glossary-term("Save state")
#para("An emulator’s snapshot of a game in progress. It is a different facility from the game’s own save.")
#glossary-term("Screen saver")
#para("An animation that fills the screen. On the PiForma, the Flying Toasters are a screen saver you start yourself; nothing starts on its own when the computer is idle. Hold the Apple logo for about six seconds to stop it.")
#glossary-term("USB hub")
#para("An accessory that provides several USB connections from one computer port.")
#glossary-term("Wi-Fi")
#para("The wireless network connection, managed by the operating system’s network tools. Bluetooth and the mouse receiver do not provide it.")
